AIM: To find the position of a number using linear search operation in c.

ALGORITHM:

Step 1: Start
Step 2: Declare variables n, key, flag
Step 3: Set flag = 0
Step 4: Read the value of n (number of elements)
Step 5: Declare an array of size n
Step 6: Input n elements into the array
Step 7: Read the value of key (element to search)
Step 8: Repeat for i = 0 to n - 1
  • If arr[i] == key, then
   – Set flag = 1
   – Print the position i + 1
   – Break the loop
Step 9: If flag == 0, then print "Element not found"
Step 10: Stop

CODE:

#include<stdio.h>
int main(){
  int n,key,flag=0;
  printf("Enter number of elements: ");
  scanf("%d",&n);
  int arr[n];
  printf("Enter %d elements: \n",n);
  for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
    scanf("%d",&arr[i]);
  }
  printf("enter the element to search");
  scanf("%d",&key);
  for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
    if(arr[i]==key){
    flag=1;
    printf("Element %d found at position %d\n",key,i+1);
    break;
    }
  }
  if(flag==0){
  printf("element %d not found",key);
  }
}
